/security-review — loop U5, round 3 — range 4ea824e..f3f5fdf — 2026-09-19

NO FINDINGS on f3f5fdf (range 4ea824e..f3f5fdf). Nothing newly added meets the >80%-exploitable bar.

(1) `store_identity` read (src/modules/git.rs:266-275): `store` is `common` (identity_root:245 — `normalise(git_dir.join(commondir))`, attacker-chosen) or a prefix of it (superproject:289), so `<parent>` is any directory the pointer/commondir chain can name — same reach round 1 already noted. The file's contents go only through `gitdir_pointer` and an `==` against `store` (272-273); the result is one bool that picks `parent` vs `store` as identity (274), both of which are paths the attacker already supplied, shown only via `parent_base` (last two components, 357-364) or the raw root in `--doctor`. No byte of `<parent>/.git` is disclosed. A `.git` directory there fails `read_to_string` → `None` → store stands alone; a symlinked `.git` is read but still only compared.

(2) `superproject()` (283-291): `is_store` (260-262) now matches any dot-name or `*.git` component, so e.g. commondir `../../.ssh/modules/x` yields store `~/.ssh` and `origin_url` then reads `~/.ssh/config` (299). This is not an escape: `store` is `parts[..=i]`, a strict prefix of the path the attacker's commondir already named, and the attacker could already point `common` at `~/.ssh` directly via commondir with no superproject match at all. Disclosure from any such `config` remains only a `url` value under an exact `[remote "origin"]` header, post-`classify` (authority incl. credentials dropped at 331). `Component::CurDir`/`ParentDir` cannot reach `is_store` on an absolute path because `normalise` (405-419) removes them; on a relative `..` store, `file_name()` is `None` (267) and `parent_base` returns `None` → no segment.

(3) `config_value` (327-338) now cuts at the first `#`/`;` anywhere; a cut only shortens the string, and quotes are still stripped first (330-334), so a credentialed URL still hits `rsplit_once('@')` at 331 with the authority discarded before the path is kept. Header cut at first `]` (306) affects only `in_origin`; header text never reaches output. The name still passes `super::sanitize` at src/modules/render/segments.rs:55 and `--doctor` still goes through `field()`/`sanitize_report`.

(4) Panics: `config_value` — `find` returns a char boundary or `None` → `value[..end]` safe on `""`, `"#"`, `"\""`. Header — `split_once(']')` in an `and_then`, `unwrap_or` after. `superproject` — `parts[i]` with `i` from `0..parts.len()`, `parts[..=i]` in range. `store_identity` — `let ... else` on `file_name`/`parent`. No `unwrap`/`expect`/indexing added outside tests.

(5) No subprocess or `canonicalize` added; `run_bounded` callers remain the pre-existing `ahead_count`/`dirty_counts`; `canonicalize` appears only in doc comments (225, 400).
